# Authorization decided on the raw request url string (CWE-551 code side). A
# guard that branches on request.url / req.url to decide access is fragile:
# with Fastify path-normalization the url is canonicalised AFTER the guard, so
# non-canonical paths slip through. Pairs with KEUR-NEST-012 (the adapter
# config). (promoted from the mestjs corpus).
id: KEUR-NEST-013
title: Authorization decision taken on the raw request url (NestJS guard)
category: security
severity: warning
engine: multiline
window: 20
action: warn
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .ts
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ node_modules/ dist/ build/ _spec/
patterns:
  # A url value from req.url/request.url is tested with a path method
  # (startsWith/includes/indexOf/match) to decide access. Covers the direct
  # req.url.startsWith('/admin') form and the "const url = req.url; …
  # url.startsWith('/admin')" form within the window.
  - regex: (?s)(?:req|request)\.url\b.{0,600}?\.(?:startsWith|includes|indexOf|match)\s*\(
    message: "Authorization branches on the raw request url (url.startsWith('/admin') …). The url is attacker-shaped and, under Fastify path-normalization, canonicalised AFTER the guard — bypassable (CWE-551). Decide on an authenticated role/permission claim, not the url string; keep guards route-bound via @UseGuards."
confidence: 0.6
fix: "Authorize on request.user.role / a permission claim; bind the guard to the route with @UseGuards instead of inspecting the url."
